        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "8a2f5124-f4d3-57c3-8b28-2039ef824c1b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Leon Uris\n- Products: Armageddon: A Novel of Berlin, Exodus, Trinity, The Haj\n- Places: Berlin, Germany, East Berlin, East Germany\n- Events: World War II, Berlin Airlift\n- Topics: historical fiction, post-World War II history, Palestinian Arab family history\n\nFacts:\n- Leon Uris was born on August 3, 1924, and Leon Uris became an American author known for historical fiction.\n- Armageddon: A Novel of Berlin is a novel by Leon Uris about post-World War II Berlin and Germany.\n- Armageddon: A Novel of Berlin vividly depicts the Berlin Airlift and the interactions among people from five nations, including the three major Western Allies and the Soviet occupiers of East Berlin and East Germany.\n- Exodus was published in 1958 and was one of Leon Uris's two bestselling books.\n- Trinity was published in 1976 and was one of Leon Uris's two bestselling books.\n- The Haj was published in 1984 by Leon Uris and follows a Palestinian Arab family through the area's historic events of the 1920s–1950s as witnessed by Ishmael, the youngest son.\n- Leon Uris died on June 21, 2003.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
